# Astra assistant — data isolation

## Rule

Astra AI may use **all** of the signed-in user’s Life OS data. It must **never** receive or be able to answer with another user’s data or a whole-database dump.

## Must

- Pass only `userId` from the verified access token into context loaders.
- Keep conversation / message queries filtered by `user_id`.
- Keep `buildPrivacyBoundary(userId)` on every chat completion.
- When adding entities, always include `user_id` ownership checks (`findOwned*`).

## Must not

- Query without `userId` / `user_id` for AI context.
- Accept a client-supplied “target user id” for context.
- Log or send other users’ payloads to Groq.
- Treat `app-map.ts` as a substitute for user records (map = UI; context builders = data).
